            <ArticleTitle>One year in review 2017: fibromyalgia.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>6-12</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Fibromyalgia (FM) is a complex syndrome characterised by chronic pain, fatigue and functional symptoms. Widespread pain is often its most typical feature, whereas other manifestations may be associated to various extents. Its aetiopathogenesis is still a matter of debate, but various pharmacological and non-pharmacological therapies are currently available for its treatment. We review the literature concerning the most recent findings relating to the aetiopathogenesis, assessment and treatment of FM published between January 2016 and January 2017.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
